Revert the scdc_present gating on HDMI SCDC reads/writes.

Upstream commit 3471b9a31ce352ffb343cf02a991261880aac3a7
("drm/amd/display: Rework HDMI data channel reads", kernel 7.2 / v6.18) added
a new struct dc_edid_caps.scdc_present flag and made BOTH read_scdc_caps()
(link_detection.c) and write_scdc_data() (link_ddc.c) return early whenever it
is false.

The commit that actually populates that flag from the parsed EDID —
"drm/amd/display: Improve HDMI info retrieval", which adds
populate_hdmi_info_from_connector() and does
    edid_caps->scdc_present = hdmi->scdc.supported;
in dm_helpers_parse_edid_caps() — is a SEPARATE later patch that is not in this
kernel yet. So scdc_present is stuck at false for every sink, SCDC scrambling /
TMDS_CONFIG is never programmed, and any HDMI link that needs it (>340 MHz TMDS
character rate: 4K, high-refresh; and DP->HDMI PCON paths through a USB-C dock)
comes up misconfigured. Symptom on saruman (Ryzen AI 9 365 / Radeon 880M,
DCN 3.5): the connector reports "connected", HPD works, but nothing is ever
displayed and the compositor never gets a usable output — on the physical HDMI
port and on the dock's DP->HDMI output alike. No error is logged; it is a
silent misconfiguration. Physical HDMI last worked on kernel 7.1.5
(generation 446), which predates 3471b9a31ce3.

This drops only the two guard hunks, restoring the unconditional pre-7.2
behaviour (always read SCDC caps, always write SCDC data on HDMI signals — DP
is unaffected, both call sites are HDMI-only). The scdc_present struct field is
left in place so nothing else fails to build.

Drop this patch once the kernel packaged in nixpkgs also carries the
"Improve HDMI info retrieval" commit that sets edid_caps.scdc_present
(grep the kernel source for `edid_caps->scdc_present =`). See maintenance.md.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/link_detection.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/link_detection.c
@@ -265,10 +265,6 @@ static void read_scdc_caps(struct ddc_service *ddc_service,
 	uint8_t slave_address = HDMI_SCDC_ADDRESS;
 	uint8_t offset = HDMI_SCDC_MANUFACTURER_OUI;
 
-	if (ddc_service->link->local_sink &&
-		!ddc_service->link->local_sink->edid_caps.scdc_present)
-		return;
-
 	link_query_ddc_data(ddc_service, slave_address, &offset,
 			sizeof(offset), sink->scdc_caps.manufacturer_OUI.byte,
 			sizeof(sink->scdc_caps.manufacturer_OUI.byte));
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_ddc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_ddc.c
@@ -582,4 +582,3 @@
 	if (ddc_service->link->local_sink &&
-		(ddc_service->link->local_sink->edid_caps.panel_patch.skip_scdc_overwrite ||
-		!ddc_service->link->local_sink->edid_caps.scdc_present))
+		ddc_service->link->local_sink->edid_caps.panel_patch.skip_scdc_overwrite)
 		return;
